@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Información
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Estado de la API
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Registrar a Ana (primer uso: devuelve 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Torres",
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Registrar a Luis para probar un segundo usuario
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Luis Pérez",
  "email": "luis@example.com",
  "password": "otra frase de acceso segura"
}

### Intentar registrar el mismo correo (esperado: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Otra Ana",
  "email": "ANA@EXAMPLE.COM",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Datos de registro no válidos (esperado: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "correo-invalido",
  "password": "corta"
}

### Intentar asignar el rol admin durante el registro (esperado: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Usuario no autorizado",
  "email": "rol@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura",
  "role": "admin"
}

### Login correcto de Ana (esperado: 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "ANA@EXAMPLE.COM",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Login con contraseña incorrecta (esperado: 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "contraseña incorrecta"
}

### Login con usuario inexistente (esperado: mismo 401 y mensaje)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "nadie@example.com",
  "password": "contraseña incorrecta"
}

### Listar tareas
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### Filtrar por estado
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?status=in_progress
Accept: application/json

### Filtrar por prioridad
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?priority=high
Accept: application/json

### Consultar una tarea
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Accept: application/json

### Crear una tarea
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Preparar práctica",
  "description": "Completar el CRUD con MySQL",
  "status": "pending",
  "priority": "high",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15"
}

### Crear una tarea mínima
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Revisar documentación"
}

### Sustituir una tarea
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Preparar entorno actualizado",
  "description": "Revisar Node.js, npm y MySQL",
  "status": "completed",
  "priority": "medium",
  "dueDate": null
}

### Modificar parcialmente una tarea
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "status": "completed"
}

### Eliminar una tarea
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/2

### Identificador no válido
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/abc
Accept: application/json

### Tarea inexistente
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/999999
Accept: application/json

### Datos no válidos
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "status": "terminada",
  "priority": "urgente",
  "dueDate": "15/10/2026"
}

### JSON incorrecto
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Falta cerrar el objeto"
